// Running work at the same time. Tasks share nothing: what a task is given is
// a copy, so tasks can't change each other's data.

// Calls `f` on every element at the same time, and keeps the results in
// order. Stops at the first failure.
fn map[T, U, !E](xs: [T], f: fn(T) -> U ! E) -> [U] ! E
  ex task.map([1, 2, 3], |x| x * 2) == [2, 4, 6]
